# Agent worktrees. CONTRIBUTING tells you to make one per session, and the
# example path puts it here — so these accumulate, and unignored they bury the
# real untracked files in `git status`. Only the `worktrees/` subdirectory is
# ignored, so a future committed `.claude/settings.json` still shows up.
#
# Prefer a path OUTSIDE the repo. A worktree nested in the working tree is one
# `git clean -fdx` away from being deleted with everything in it, and it holds
# its branch hostage: `main` checked out at `.codex/worktrees/issue49` makes
# `git switch main` fail in this checkout with "already used by worktree".
.claude/worktrees/
.codex/worktrees/
